      {
        "t": "chr",
        "v": [
          "This module checks whether each extracted data column is documented in a codebook or README, and flags documented variables that never appear in the data.",
          "We examined 1 codebook/README/label source and 12 data columns across 1 file.",
          "#### Column Documentation",
          "::: {.panel-tabset}\n\n## affect.csv\n\n\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(Column = c(\"id\", \"PANAS1\", \"PANAS10\", \"PANAS2\", \n\"PANAS3\", \"PANAS4\", \"PANAS5\", \"PANAS6\", \"PANAS7\", \"PANAS8\", \"PANAS9\", \n\"PANAS_total\"), Documented = c(\"no\", \"yes\", \"yes\", \"yes\", \"yes\", \n\"yes\", \"yes\", \"yes\", \"yes\", \"yes\", \"yes\", \"yes\"), Label = c(NA, \n\"Affect item 1\", \"Affect item 10\", \"Affect item 2\", \"Affect item 3\", \n\"Affect item 4\", \"Affect item 5\", \"Affect item 6\", \"Affect item 7\", \n\"Affect item 8\", \"Affect item 9\", \"Total affect score\"), \"Codebook Variable\" = c(NA, \n\"PANAS1\", \"PANAS10\", \"PANAS2\", \"PANAS3\", \"PANAS4\", \"PANAS5\", \n\"PANAS6\", \"PANAS7\", \"PANAS8\", \"PANAS9\", \"PANAS_total\"), Source = c(NA, \n\"codebook.csv\", \"codebook.csv\", \"codebook.csv\", \"codebook.csv\", \n\"codebook.csv\", \"codebook.csv\", \"codebook.csv\", \"codebook.csv\", \n\"codebook.csv\", \"codebook.csv\", \"codebook.csv\"), Status = c(\"unlabelled\", \n\"labelled\", \"labelled\", \"labelled\", \"labelled\", \"labelled\", \"labelled\", \n\"labelled\", \"labelled\", \"labelled\", \"labelled\", \"labelled\")), row.names = c(NA, \n12L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 25, FALSE)\n```\n\n\n:::",
          "#### Scales",
          "We detected 1 column group (by shared abbreviation) that look like scales; 1 was matched to a named instrument from the paper text or dictionary. Groups we could not name are listed too — they are real scale-like column families whose instrument the manuscript did not identify. Identified scales are exported in the OpenScales OSD structure.",
          "\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(File = \"affect.csv\", Abbrev = \"PANAS\", Columns = 10L, \n    \"Max item\" = \"10\", Scale = \"Positive and Negative Affect Schedule\", \n    Confidence = \"high\", Source = \"matched\"), row.names = c(NA, \n-1L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 40, FALSE)\n```\n",
          "#### Tasks",
          "**1 task named in the manuscript has no matching data.** The trial-level data may not be shared, may live in a file we could not read, or may use column names we did not recognise. Sharing trial-level data (one row per trial, with condition, response time and accuracy) would let the task be verified:",
          "- Positive and Negative Affect Scale",
          "LLM model 'mock/rv' reviewed ambiguous cases (parsed 0 files, matched 0 columns, merged 0 labels)."
        ]
